  "body": "Establish the Lab 3 engineering contract and test plan before runtime feature implementation. The contract now preserves Lab 2 Requester API behavior and Zen Green styling, defines Staff/Admin permissions and missing API details, and maps 56 ACs to 107 planned tests.\n\nThe audit corrections also remove conflicting pipeline copies, exclude Department management, align AGENTS.md with Lab 3 staging, and correct the premature P02 Complete claim. P02 remains blocked on executable test DB/upload isolation; later product and release gates remain Planned.\n\nValidation:\n- Documentation consistency: 56 unique/mapped ACs, 107 Planned test rows, correct reverse mapping and FR/BR references, 64 valid JSON examples, 17 permitted/47 rejected status pairs, existing theme tokens matched.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- `npm run test:client`: 37 passed, 0 failed/skipped (Lab 1–2 regression only); raw output in `artifacts/lab-03/contract-review-20260913/client.txt`.\n- Server/Playwright not run: current setup uses shared DB/uploads and overwrites existing screenshots; implement and verify LCP-01/HARNESS-01 first. Builds not rerun for this documentation-only change.\n\nReview scope: the full `docs/lab3-contract` branch (P00/P01 documentation, P02 plan, and correction commit `11307f3`). No application source, dependencies, applied migrations or user data are changed. No Lab 3 product test is claimed passing.\n\nPlease review the contract and traceability before merging into `lab3-staging`. A peer reviewer must approve and perform the merge. The linked Issue was created after the documentation commits; workflow timing is recorded without implying otherwise.\n\nRelated issue: #34. Issue #34 is explicitly linked as a closing issue in Development, verified through GitHub; the PR targets lab3-staging.\n",
